Q: Using f:param inside o:graphicImage A: <p>The <code>&lt;f:param&gt;</code> inside <code>&lt;p:graphicImage&gt;</code> is a <a href="https://stackoverflow.com/questions/8207325/display-dynamic-image-from-database-with-pgraphicimage-and-streamedcontent">PrimeFaces-specific trick</a> to get the <code>StreamedContent</code> thing to work "as expected".</p>

<p>The <code>&lt;o:graphicImage&gt;</code> doesn't support it (neither does standard <code>&lt;h:graphicImage&gt;</code>). Just pass it as EL method argument the usual way. It ends up in more clean code.</p>

<pre><code>&lt;o:graphicImage value="#{bean.getImage(data.id)}" /&gt;
</code></pre>

<p></p>

<pre><code>public InputStream getImage(Long dataId) {
    // ...
}
</code></pre>

<p>See also code examples in <a href="http://showcase.omnifaces.org/components/graphicImage" rel="nofollow noreferrer">documentation</a>.</p>
